epublic of Turkey wanted to draw a  line between the old order and the new  and he did this in 1923 by formally  changing the name of Constantinople to  Istanbul to match what it was already  called by the Turkish people and he  asked that all of the nations respect  this change and start calling the  Turkish capital Istanbul from then on  they did not most major European nations  kept calling at what they had done  previously in of the world's major  powers it was only the United States  that acknowledged the change and so the  Turkish now had some difficulty since  they wanted to be taken seriously and so  to force the issue in 1930 Turkey passed  a new postal law which forbid the postal  service from delivering letters  addressed to Constantinople and this  worked which  is why most nations officially refer to  the city as Istanbul now except for the  Greeks I hope you enjoyed this episode  and the special thanks to all my patreon  supporters James vis Annette  Marvin casts out a man of culture Kelly  moneymaker  Danny Meloni Jon viscous Rob Waterhouse  mo Aaron the white James Castaneda  Gustav Swan Jordan long ray Marcus Ozma  spinning three plates cooling Castleman  filled oink oink Rashid Ali David  Silverman easy Maggie packs Kowski  Spencer Lightfoot of Winston K word  Robert Wetzel Lexy Schwinn Anthony  Beckett and Skye Chappell personally I  prefer Mick Lagarde
 

